index 0000000..e6f7e9c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-none-zero-3e7a9d1c5b20f684.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    ``Retrying(wait=None)``, ``wait=0`` and ``wait=sum([])`` mean "no wait"
+    again. Retrying after a failure raised ``TypeError: 'NoneType' object is
+    not callable`` (or ``'int' object is not callable``) instead of retrying
+    without a delay. This applies to both ``Retrying`` and ``AsyncRetrying``.
diff --git a/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-plain-callable-8c4f2e6a1d9b0537.yaml b/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-plain-callable-8c4f2e6a1d9b0537.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f307412
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-plain-callable-8c4f2e6a1d9b0537.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    A plain callable can again be added to a wait strategy with ``+``:
+    ``my_callable + wait_fixed(1)`` builds a ``wait_combine`` that sums both.
+    ``wait_combine`` now passes the retry state to each strategy positionally,
+    so plain callables may name their parameter anything.
